    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the only executable test class is `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper). `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-duplicate flag for `POST /api/owners`. A newly created owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while having a different telephone is still created, and returns `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the earliest matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges, following the project's OfficeFloor-function conventions:\n\n- **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function): after `BuildOwner`, iterates existing owners; matches case-insensitive `lastName` + equal non-blank `postcode` + differing canonical telephone (so a hard duplicate isn't flagged here), picks the lowest matching id, and sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` on the entity so they persist and are read back on `GET`.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`**: inserted a `possibleDuplicate` step between `build` and `customerCode` (under `transaction` governance like its neighbors).\n- **`Owner.java`**: added `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with getters/setters, mirroring `namesakeCount`/`bulkSignupWarning`.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema; the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` auto-maps them by name (no mapper edit needed).\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres): added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns; updated the positional owner seed INSERTs in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the only dialect using positional VALUES) with two trailing `NULL`s.\n\nThe target test `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite pass.",
